(>> 5.4 University Review & Examination Questions) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Q1: Contrast malloc\(\), calloc\(\), realloc\(\), and free\(\) in C regarding their) Tj
T*
(arguments, initialization, and error handling.) Tj
T*
(Answer: \(1\) malloc\(size_t size\): Takes single argument specifying total bytes. Allocates) Tj
T*
(contiguous memory on Heap without initialization \(contents are garbage\). Returns void*) Tj
T*
(pointer to first byte, or NULL on failure. \(2\) calloc\(size_t num, size_t size\): Takes) Tj
T*
(two arguments: number of elements and size of each. Allocates memory and clears all bits) Tj
T*
(to ZERO. Useful for arrays and numeric buffers to prevent garbage bugs. Returns NULL on) Tj
T*
(failure. \(3\) realloc\(void *ptr, size_t new_size\): Resizes an existing heap block pointed) Tj
T*
(to by ptr. May expand in-place or relocate the block to a new heap location, preserving) Tj
T*
(existing data up to minimum of old and new size. If ptr is NULL, behaves like) Tj
T*
(malloc\(new_size\). Returns pointer to reallocated memory or NULL on failure. \(4\)) Tj
T*
(free\(void *ptr\): Deallocates previously allocated heap memory, returning it to runtime) Tj
T*
(heap pool. Does not zero out pointer, creating dangling pointer if not explicitly set to) Tj
T*
(NULL.) Tj
T*
(* Q2: Explain the concepts of Dangling Pointers and Memory Leaks with code examples) Tj
T*
(and mitigation techniques.) Tj
T*
(Answer: A Dangling Pointer points to memory that has already been deallocated \(freed\) or) Tj
T*
(gone out of scope. Example: 'int *p = \(int*\)malloc\(sizeof\(int\)\); free\(p\); *p = 50; //) Tj
T*
(UNDEFINED BEHAVIOR'. Mitigation: Always assign 'p = NULL;' immediately following) Tj
T*
('free\(p\);' and verify 'if \(p != NULL\)' before dereferencing. A Memory Leak occurs when) Tj
T*
(dynamically allocated heap memory is no longer referenced by any pointer but was never) Tj
T*
(released with free\(\). Example: 'void leak\(\) { int *p = \(int*\)malloc\(100\); } // Pointer p) Tj
T*
(destroyed on exit, but 100 bytes remain stranded on Heap'. Over time, leaks accumulate) Tj
T*
(and cause program termination due to Out-Of-Memory errors. Mitigation: Always pair every) Tj
T*
(malloc/calloc call with a corresponding free\(\) invocation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
